  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will learn how to write terms that include rational exponents as radicals and vice versa.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Simplify radical expressions with even and odd indexes.</item>
  <item>Rewrite expressions with rational exponents as roots.</item>
  <item>Use properties for exponents with rational exponents.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>5.2.1: Perfect Squares Revisited</item>
  <item>5.2.2: The nth Root
    <list id="list-00003">
      <item>5.2.2: Self Check </item>
      <item>5.2.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item>5.2.3: Radicals and Rational Exponents 
    <list id="list-00004">
      <item>5.2.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>5.2.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item>5.2.4: Properties of Exponents with Rationals</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>5.2.5: Practice</item>
  <item>5.2.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
